    "note": "candidate-001 — first cut of @m0saic/alpine/treemap/v1 (the 9th + FINAL Alpine template, completing the pack). A squarified treemap in the white card: value-sized rounded tiles packed to fill the card (squarified algorithm → balanced aspect ratios, no slivers), each labelled top-left with its name + share (% by default). Tiles fade in biggest→smallest. Built on the donut/heatmap placeRects model (absolute tight rects on the 4px lattice, grid as a full-canvas extraLayer → no quantization). Palette cycles ALPINE_PALETTE (per-item color override supported); label contrast auto-flips (white on saturated tiles). Long names truncate with an ellipsis; labels hide on tiles too small to hold them. Validated valid at 1280x800.",
    "question": "First look at the Alpine treemap. Scrub it — tiles fade in biggest→smallest. Checking: (1) the squarified packing — do the tiles read as balanced rounded cards (no slivers), and is the gap right? (2) the label layout (name + % top-left), contrast on each tile, and the small-tile hide threshold; (3) palette + corner radius; (4) the fade cascade. Open Q: valueMode default percent — keep, or show raw value? I will iterate one nudge at a time.",
